WEBVTT

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:36.240
<b>Kagura is broke, which is why she doesn't have a cell phone! But she wants to join in the text messaging fun!</b>

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:41.080
<b>Kagura manages to get her hands on a cell phone and makes an unexpected text pal!!</b>

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:45.090
So, that show was the best!

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:49.080
Yep, Kadono Takuzo did a great job as the boyfriend.

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:51.170
Kagura-chan, that's a different show.

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:53.010
Maybe I should watch it.

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:55.170
But I want to start from the beginning.

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:56.990
We can watch it together at my house.

00:01:56.990 --> 00:01:58.150
I recorded all the episodes.

00:01:58.150 --> 00:01:59.040
Yes!

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:01.790
I can eat all the Happy Turns I want at Marippe's place!

00:02:01.790 --> 00:02:03.180
That's what you're interested in?

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:05.720
I'll text you once I find out which day will work.

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:07.180
Text?

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:09.560
Oh, Kagura-chan doesn't have a cell phone.

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:13.730
I'll let you know in person once I get her text.

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:18.480
Bye, Kagura-chan, Marippe.

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:20.940
Saki-chan, text me your opinion of the show after you watch it.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:32.630
<b>It Would Take Too Much Effort to Make This Title Sound Like a Text Message Subject</b>

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:34.660
Sadaemon!

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:35.800
Listen!

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:38.640
Giako and Suneko were showing off their cell phones!

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:43.430
These days, even babies are born with cell phones
dangling from their umbilical cords!

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:45.930
You never learn, Kagura-chan.

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:48.930
Cell phones are useful, especially at work,

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:53.710
but you'll need to check Gin-chan's four-dimensional pouch.

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:55.740
But I can't just ask him directly.

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:59.760
It would be so much easier if I could just text him.

00:03:01.270 --> 00:03:05.400
You don't need texting when you can
understand each other through your hearts.

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:12.300
I'm sure you can understand how hard a cell phone is on the wallet.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:17.900
So shut that foul mouth of yours and sleep in the closet with me.

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:22.180
Don't be fooled, Kagura-chan.

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:25.180
Someone hacked into me and took control.

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:26.830
You can drop the act now.

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:27.740
Who sent you?

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.030
Are you a spy from the Steel Troops?

00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:32.560
Hey, don't say that! Riruru is our friend!

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:35.440
Can't you talk to each other directly?!

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:38.550
Why are you going through this convoluted process?!

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:41.090
If you have something to say, say it to his face!

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:42.640
Mama, listen!

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:43.850
Who's your mama?!

00:03:43.850 --> 00:03:44.990
Though my face is kind of similar!

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:48.560
We're the only ones who don't have cell phones!

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:52.260
At this rate, Odd Jobs will fall behind the times!

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:53.000
Did you hear that?

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:54.780
Enough of that!

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:58.250
Our bamboo-copter is running on fumes
after paying for you and Sadademon's food.

00:03:58.660 --> 00:04:02.130
I don't need a cell phone to know how everyone feels.

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:05.190
For example, Sadaemon wants to poop right now.

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:08.860
And Mama read my mind and prepared a newspaper.

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:10.630
So we don't need cell phones!

00:04:10.630 --> 00:04:12.640
That's just a daily practice!

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:14.650
If you insist on being selfish,

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:17.060
you can use the Anywhere Door to join a family anywhere else!

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:18.070
Shut up!

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:21.360
I'll use the Air Cannon to knock off that funny hair!

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:22.450
See? You know what I'm thinking!

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:25.240
I was getting sick of this round hair!

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:27.950
Uh, something's come out...

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:28.030
Sadaemon, drag stupid Papa into your four-dimensional pocket!

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:28.730
Huh?

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:31.330
...of Sadaemon's four-dimensional pocket.

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:34.310
Cell phones...

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:37.210
<b>Doll House</b>

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:37.790
I checked the data,

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:41.090
but the phones were busted to begin with, so I can't identify the owners.

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:45.840
The addresses were all changed to ne.jpuripuri.

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:48.130
Well, they were covered in poop.

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:50.930
Uh, why would that change the addresses?

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:53.200
So? Can we use them now?

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:54.960
You can't make calls.

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:57.620
The phone will add a puripuri to the end of everything you say.

00:04:57.620 --> 00:04:59.190
Isn't that more impressive than a working cell phone?!

00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:03.890
You only have enough money for me to fix the texting function.

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:09.970
Yay!

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:12.420
Thanks, Gramps!

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:13.950
Thanks, Sadaemon!

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:19.210
I don't want to carry around a cell phone that was covered in poop.

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:22.410
Humans are always carrying around poop.

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:24.960
The only difference is that it'll be in your hand instead of inside your body.

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:25.880
Give me those.

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:28.390
<b>Odd Jobs</b>

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:28.390
That should do it.

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:32.140
Now, we'll always be together, no matter where we go.

00:05:32.920 --> 00:05:35.870
You have to carry this everywhere, okay?

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:37.140
Promise.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:42.900
If you get lonely, you can text me!

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:55.070
Man, why is someone calling me this early?

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:58.080
Good morning. It's a beautiful morning.

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:07.720
What? It's already morning...?

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:10.050
Good night. Sweet dreams.

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:13.640
<b>Bathroom</b>

00:06:19.250 --> 00:06:21.400
Good morning. Your poop is very smooth today.

00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:26.900
Okay, I locked the door today...

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:28.140
Huh?

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:31.910
Good morning. Your poop is even smoother today.

00:06:34.510 --> 00:06:36.450
There it is! That's the cat!

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:37.910
I'll circle around!

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:39.580
You kids stay on its tail!

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:44.750
Kagura-chan!

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:46.460
Hey! Are you okay?!

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:51.050
I'm okay.

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:53.180
<b>Snack Otose</b>

00:06:53.910 --> 00:06:55.930
Could you pass me the Kleenex?

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:57.770
Does this come in an M?

00:06:58.230 --> 00:07:00.480
That M is for Michael.

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:03.110
Not that Michael. Michael Douglas.

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:05.440
Talk to our faces!

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:08.840
Why do you have to text every little stupid thing?!

00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:12.240
And she's not even talking to us?!

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:14.440
She's talking to a clerk in some clothing store!

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:18.450
No, this isn't a clothing store. It's a Michael store.

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:21.400
Hey!

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:22.960
Cut it out!

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:25.070
Who cares if it's M or Michael?!

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:26.090
This is a surprise.

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:29.170
I wouldn't have expected her to be so enthusiastic about a cell phone.

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:30.630
This is more than being enthusiastic!

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:33.100
She sends us pointless updates every five minutes!

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:34.040
I'm sick of it!

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:37.600
Girls love to chitchat through letters and the like.

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:39.850
When I was in school...

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:41.470
Pass this to Catherine.

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:43.100
<b>Challenge</b>

00:07:41.470 --> 00:07:43.480
How long ago was this?!

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:45.310
And did everyone hate you?!

00:07:46.130 --> 00:07:50.990
Sometimes, it's easier to say things through
a written medium than talking face-to-face.

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:54.510
This may be the real Kagura-sama.

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:56.680
Are you replying to her?

00:07:56.680 --> 00:07:58.420
We can't do that.

00:07:58.420 --> 00:08:01.260
She's using text messages to talk to us now.

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:05.000
It's possible that she keeps sending
texts because she's waiting for a reply.

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:09.730
Men always act cool and never say what needs to be said.

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:12.680
They expect other people to know how they feel.

00:08:13.310 --> 00:08:16.780
But sometimes, women just want to hear those words.

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:20.230
Just send her a nice text.

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:22.140
Here, this is your chance!

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:23.910
Answer the phone!

00:08:23.910 --> 00:08:26.060
Respond with, "I'm actually a pedo!"

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:27.400
I'll kill you, you rotten banana!

00:08:27.950 --> 00:08:29.550
Shinpachi, it's all yours.

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:30.650
Gi-Gin-san!

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:32.320
Well? What did it say?

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:33.320
Move it, hag!

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:34.620
I want to see!

00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:36.320
Hey, don't look at my phone!

00:08:37.090 --> 00:08:38.830
Hmm? Where are you right now?

00:08:39.260 --> 00:08:43.120
Wasn't she here just a moment ago? Why is she asking this?

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:46.330
Huh? Now there's a text from Gin-san.

00:08:46.570 --> 00:08:48.400
Shut up! I'm at a pachinko-

00:08:48.740 --> 00:08:50.840
It's cut off.

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:53.700
Was he replying to Kagura-chan?

00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:56.000
He accidentally hit reply to all.

00:08:56.240 --> 00:08:58.600
And he wrote his message in the subject.

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:01.920
So he's actually replying to Kagura.

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:03.150
Your wallpaper is gross!

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:03.930
Shut up!

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:05.670
Rotten banana on the ground!

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:06.850
<b>You have a new message.</b>

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:06.850
Oh, there's another one.

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:11.610
<b>Where are you right now?</b>

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:09.630
It's the same message again.

00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:11.610
Wait, is something wrong?

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:13.860
Huh? I just noticed...

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:15.860
This isn't from Kagura-chan...

00:09:16.810 --> 00:09:18.560
Who sent this?

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:21.580
<b>Return the cell phone.</b>

00:09:23.130 --> 00:09:24.510
Tell me where you are at once.

00:09:24.510 --> 00:09:28.130
If you leak the information in those phones, you're dead.

00:09:28.350 --> 00:09:30.460
It's from the owner of this phone!

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:32.350
They're threatening to kill you...

00:09:32.350 --> 00:09:34.500
It must be someone dangerous.

00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:37.340
What kind of information is in this phone?!

00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:38.910
I don't know!

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:43.220
Gengai-san said that the phones were busted and there wasn't any data left!

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:45.600
In any case, you should contact Gintoki-sama and Kagura-sama.

00:09:47.550 --> 00:09:48.600
It's from Gin-san!

00:09:48.930 --> 00:09:51.130
Did they find him already?!

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:53.770
Shut up! I'm at a pachinko

00:09:53.770 --> 00:09:55.080
parlor playing with balls!

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:58.240
He's picking up from where his message cut off!

00:09:58.590 --> 00:10:00.090
What is he doing?!

00:10:00.090 --> 00:10:03.040
He just gave away his location to everyone!

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:05.950
That means the owner will head straight to the parlor?

00:10:05.950 --> 00:10:07.710
Of course not!

00:10:08.390 --> 00:10:09.850
Oh, there's another text.

00:10:09.850 --> 00:10:11.370
It must be from the owner!

00:10:11.370 --> 00:10:12.350
Look at the message.

00:10:12.350 --> 00:10:13.470
I don't want to!

00:10:13.470 --> 00:10:14.670
Catherine-san, you look!

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:16.090
Screw that! Aren't you a man?!

00:10:16.090 --> 00:10:16.990
Answer the phone, hag!

00:10:16.990 --> 00:10:18.260
Who are you calling a man?!

00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:19.730
Tama-san!

00:10:19.730 --> 00:10:21.550
Wh-What does it say?

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:23.310
<b>From: Kyubei</b>

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:24.790
You're playing with balls?

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:27.270
Somebody completely different joined the conversation!

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:31.520
Did you come out of the closet?

00:10:31.750 --> 00:10:33.720
Are you going to have an operation?

00:10:33.720 --> 00:10:35.500
Can I have yours?

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:36.680
We need to talk.

00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:37.820
Please reply.

00:10:38.080 --> 00:10:39.580
What is she talking about?!

00:10:39.580 --> 00:10:41.150
What does she want to do?!

00:10:41.150 --> 00:10:42.660
There are more messages.

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:45.450
<b>From: Saigo</b>

00:10:43.390 --> 00:10:46.110
Welcome. I'm glad to hear that.

00:10:46.110 --> 00:10:49.860
Tell Pako that he can become No. 1 at my place.

00:10:49.860 --> 00:10:52.960
This has turned into a completely different
conversation in a completely different world.

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:55.000
<b>From: Tojo</b>

00:10:53.320 --> 00:10:54.430
What a coincidence.

00:10:54.430 --> 00:10:56.670
I was also playing with balls.

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:59.470
And this guy is in his own little world!

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:00.300
Ah...

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:02.800
<b>From: Zura
Sub: It's not Zura, it's Katsura</b>

00:11:00.770 --> 00:11:02.800
It appears that you're having trouble...

00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:03.800
Katsura-san!

00:11:04.060 --> 00:11:09.230
However, I assure you that I can ease your pain.

00:11:09.460 --> 00:11:11.750
Is he going to help us?!

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:15.360
<b>The Perfect Happiness Theory
The Joi Patriot Happiness Doctrine</b>

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:15.390
Join the Joi patriots and find happiness.

00:11:15.390 --> 00:11:19.460
We have a testimonial from Mrs. E who was able to find her happiness.

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:23.780
<b>Mrs. E</b>

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:23.870
I didn't think it would be so easy to become a Joi patriot.

00:11:24.770 --> 00:11:27.240
The Joi will help find your joy.

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:29.620
It's just spam!

00:11:30.030 --> 00:11:32.500
And they're getting worse!

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:34.890
Damn! This will never end!

00:11:34.890 --> 00:11:36.210
Hey, Shinpachi!

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:42.140
Gin-chan, I made a new text pal.

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:45.020
Damn! Damn!

00:11:45.020 --> 00:11:46.870
Why aren't they replying?!

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:48.480
What are they doing?!

00:11:49.760 --> 00:11:51.500
I'm about to meet my new text pal.

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:52.480
I can't wait.

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:54.360
I'll introduce you some time.

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:06.370
Kagura-chan!

00:12:06.570 --> 00:12:09.370
Whew, she finally saw my mail!

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:11.240
I'm meeting with my text pal offline.

00:12:11.240 --> 00:12:12.770
He's a very nice person!

00:12:12.770 --> 00:12:15.380
Death Cancer-san is also eager to meet you guys.

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:18.280
Uh, that's not a text pal!

00:12:18.280 --> 00:12:19.540
I guarantee it!

00:12:19.540 --> 00:12:21.780
There's nothing peaceful about his peace sign!

00:12:21.780 --> 00:12:24.640
His name is Death Cancer!

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:26.360
He got to her first!

00:12:26.360 --> 00:12:30.520
This isn't an offline meeting!
Kagura-chan's been taken hostage!

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:34.060
Your buddy is in my hands.

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:37.520
Bring the cell phones to the family restaurant on 2nd within 10 minutes.

00:12:37.740 --> 00:12:39.860
It's the owner!

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:41.670
You have 10 minutes.

00:12:41.670 --> 00:12:45.530
No one has stood before my Death Cancer (claws of death)
for 10 minutes and survived.

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:50.370
I'm sure you know what will happen if you're late. (Murder.)

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:51.560
This is bad!

00:12:51.560 --> 00:12:53.290
This guy is obviously one of those people!

00:12:53.590 --> 00:12:55.300
He's using emoticons I've never seen before!

00:12:55.300 --> 00:12:57.290
I've never seen anyone go (Murder) before!

00:12:57.940 --> 00:12:59.030
That settles it.

00:12:59.030 --> 00:13:00.920
This guy must be an assassin of some kind!

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:03.420
W-We've picked up some unbelievable cell phones!

00:13:04.240 --> 00:13:04.930
Gin-san!

00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:08.800
He must have realized the danger we're in after seeing that text!

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:11.160
Sorry, I'm at a pachinko

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:13.290
parlor playing with balls real good.

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:15.070
Could you give me ten more minutes?

00:13:15.070 --> 00:13:17.350
He still doesn't know how to use a cell phone!

00:13:17.350 --> 00:13:18.770
And he's still playing pachinko?!

00:13:18.770 --> 00:13:20.320
Doesn't he care about us?!

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:22.320
<b>From: Death Cancer</b>

00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:24.340
What do you mean, real good? (Murder.)

00:13:24.340 --> 00:13:25.300
This is really bad!

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:26.820
He's mad! It says (Murder)!

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:29.240
I'm doing so well it's like the pachinko

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:31.470
goddess of balls has blessed me!

00:13:31.470 --> 00:13:32.960
My balls are on a high!

00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:34.490
I can't stop! Can't stop!

00:13:34.490 --> 00:13:36.360
It's a miracle how his texts can sound so wrong!

00:13:36.360 --> 00:13:38.330
Stop it! Stop antagonizing him!

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:40.500
<b>From: Death Cancer</b>

00:13:39.330 --> 00:13:42.930
No one has stood before my Death Cancer (claws of death)
for 10 minutes and survived.

00:13:42.930 --> 00:13:45.420
Are you somewhere I can reach within ten minutes? (Must.)

00:13:45.420 --> 00:13:47.710
Hey! He wants to go to him now!

00:13:47.710 --> 00:13:49.850
And now it's a (Must)!

00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:51.540
Can you come to me?

00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:53.470
The name of the place is Fever.

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:56.600
<b>Pachinko Fever</b>

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:54.940
You shouldn't tell him that!

00:13:54.940 --> 00:13:56.600
Run away! Gin-san, run away!

00:13:57.080 --> 00:13:58.240
We're meeting up

00:13:58.240 --> 00:13:59.390
somewhere different.

00:13:59.390 --> 00:14:01.080
Hurry up, Shinpachi!

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:05.990
<b>Balls Fever</b>

00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:02.360
That's the wrong place!

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:03.810
He's got it wrong!

00:14:03.810 --> 00:14:06.150
We sent Death Cancer to the wrong place!

00:14:06.150 --> 00:14:10.200
<b>From: Death Cancer</b>

00:14:06.740 --> 00:14:08.490
You lied to me.

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:10.210
He's really mad in this message!

00:14:10.210 --> 00:14:12.740
There are only 30 minute and 60 minute options.

00:14:12.740 --> 00:14:15.120
There isn't a 10 minute option. (Murder.)

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:16.280
That's why he's mad?!

00:14:16.280 --> 00:14:17.620
He would rather take the 10 minute option?!

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:20.710
<b>From: Death Cancer</b>

00:14:18.240 --> 00:14:19.110
No matter then.

00:14:19.110 --> 00:14:22.510
I'll be finished in 30 minutes, so we can meet up again in 40 minutes.

00:14:22.510 --> 00:14:24.660
So you're off to your fever?!

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:27.150
Why did he even come here?!

00:14:27.150 --> 00:14:28.760
Doesn't he want his cell phones back?!

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:30.500
Oh, that's right!

00:14:30.500 --> 00:14:32.980
This is my chance to tell Kagura-chan to run away!

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:35.270
Looks like we're still meeting

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:36.930
up at the same time.

00:14:37.280 --> 00:14:39.560
Ten minutes?! He didn't even last 10 seconds!

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:41.150
How fast is this guy?!

00:14:41.270 --> 00:14:44.270
<b>From: Death Cancer</b>

00:14:41.430 --> 00:14:45.860
No one has stood before my Death Cancer (claws of death)
for 10 minutes and survived.

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:48.250
Your Death Cancer is the one that couldn't survive!

00:14:48.250 --> 00:14:49.280
Stop posing!

00:14:49.830 --> 00:14:51.100
That's the wrong place.

00:14:51.100 --> 00:14:52.410
Kagura, show him the way.

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:56.410
It's the place on the corner of 3rd where I'm always playing with balls.

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:58.040
<b>Pachinko Fever</b>

00:14:56.410 --> 00:14:58.040
You don't have to tell him this!

00:14:58.350 --> 00:14:59.770
You mean here?

00:15:00.600 --> 00:15:02.640
Nobody told you to smash his balls into a corner!

00:15:02.640 --> 00:15:05.720
Hey! Is Death Cancer-san okay!

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:09.470
<b>From: Holy Cancer
Sub: (claws of hope)</b>

00:15:06.570 --> 00:15:11.570
I feel like I just woke up from a very long nightmare.

00:15:11.570 --> 00:15:12.570
Who are you?!

00:15:12.570 --> 00:15:14.940
You're a completely different person, Holy Cancer!

00:15:14.940 --> 00:15:16.890
He's become enlightened after his balls were smashed!

00:15:17.340 --> 00:15:22.210
Forgive me... I just wanted my cell phones back.

00:15:22.530 --> 00:15:23.850
You see, those three cell phones

00:15:23.850 --> 00:15:26.530
each hold memories I can't forget...

00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:29.940
No, they hold memories I should never forget.

00:15:29.940 --> 00:15:32.450
Uh, shouldn't you tell us this after we meet up?

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:35.710
I may sound eloquent over the phone,

00:15:35.710 --> 00:15:38.650
but I'm actually a shy man who can
barely look another person in the eye,

00:15:38.650 --> 00:15:42.270
much less talk to someone face-to-face.

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:49.800
It must have been a twist of fate
that I ended up marrying such a talkative woman.

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:50.950
He's doing a flashback through a text message!

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:51.820
What's going on?!

00:15:51.820 --> 00:15:53.050
And you were a a barber?!

00:15:54.370 --> 00:16:00.020
I worked as a barber,
but I kept losing customers because I never talked much.

00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:01.060
I don't think that's why you lost customers.

00:16:01.770 --> 00:16:07.300
That was when my wife gave me a cell phone.

00:16:08.420 --> 00:16:12.450
She thought that I might be able
to speak through words, through a text message.

00:16:12.790 --> 00:16:15.680
The silent artist thing works,

00:16:15.680 --> 00:16:18.950
but you should learn to joke in front of your wife.

00:16:19.340 --> 00:16:25.200
I-I'm too old to fool around with that text messaging nonsense.

00:16:27.010 --> 00:16:30.830
Yet you're still wearing those claws of yours.

00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:34.780
The words which brought a rare smile to my wife's face

00:16:34.780 --> 00:16:39.850
ended up being my last words to her.

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:46.830
Those cell phones are filled with the words I was never able to say to her.

00:16:47.560 --> 00:16:49.960
They will never reach her,

00:16:49.960 --> 00:16:53.360
but they are still precious to me.

00:16:56.980 --> 00:16:58.620
I went to a cabaret club today!

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:00.620
I went to a pink salon today!

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:03.620
I think I'll go all the way to Yoshiwara today!

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:06.380
Your messages are stupid!

00:17:06.890 --> 00:17:09.930
How could you send these dirty texts to heaven?!

00:17:09.930 --> 00:17:11.080
You've got it wrong.

00:17:11.080 --> 00:17:14.770
I was searching for heaven, so I could reach my wife.

00:17:14.770 --> 00:17:16.890
You're headed straight to hell!

00:17:17.270 --> 00:17:20.890
Those cell phones are priceless.

00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:23.770
Could you please return them?

00:17:24.960 --> 00:17:29.810
T-Texting is a pain in the ass anyway.

00:17:29.810 --> 00:17:32.740
We're not cut out for this high-tech stuff.

00:17:33.560 --> 00:17:35.320
R-Really?!

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:36.950
Thank you so much!

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:40.620
<b>Odd Jobs</b>

00:17:38.920 --> 00:17:42.680
Now, we'll always be together, no matter where we go.

00:17:44.510 --> 00:17:46.270
Come on, Kagura-chan.

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:50.210
No way.

00:17:51.800 --> 00:17:52.800
Kagura-chan...

00:17:54.450 --> 00:17:57.440
I haven't received a text message yet.

00:17:58.730 --> 00:18:02.220
That couple is connected, even though they're far apart.

00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:03.970
Unlike us.

00:18:05.150 --> 00:18:08.320
Stop dwelling in the past, stupid old man!

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:12.110
We're the ones who aren't able to say what we need to!

00:18:12.110 --> 00:18:13.280
<b>Message Sent</b>

00:18:12.110 --> 00:18:13.650
Stupid! Stupid! Stupid!

00:18:17.140 --> 00:18:18.630
Wait, Kagura-chan!

00:18:18.870 --> 00:18:20.450
Kagura-chan!

00:18:28.790 --> 00:18:31.040
<b>Odd Jobs</b>

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:50.850
I appreciate you coming to her third anniversary.

00:18:51.530 --> 00:18:53.660
We were brought together for a reason.

00:18:53.980 --> 00:18:57.130
Well, the reason involved poop.

00:18:57.130 --> 00:18:58.540
Anyway, I'm sorry.

00:18:58.540 --> 00:19:00.820
Kagura-chan still has that phone.

00:19:01.580 --> 00:19:03.120
I'll make sure that she returns it.

00:19:03.380 --> 00:19:04.890
It's okay.

00:19:04.890 --> 00:19:07.260
She helped me realize something.

00:19:07.260 --> 00:19:10.380
I wasn't doing it for my wife's sake.

00:19:10.380 --> 00:19:13.880
I was trying to make myself feel better.

00:19:14.430 --> 00:19:17.310
I'll stop sending text messages to myself.

00:19:17.740 --> 00:19:24.500
I'm sure that my wife was hoping
I would learn to speak with friends face-to-face.

00:19:26.390 --> 00:19:30.830
So I'll send the one final message that I've always wanted to send,

00:19:30.830 --> 00:19:32.400
and that will be that.

00:19:35.370 --> 00:19:38.980
Okay, I've said my goodbyes.

00:19:39.720 --> 00:19:41.410
Take good care of them.

00:19:41.850 --> 00:19:42.460
Huh?

00:19:42.850 --> 00:19:44.240
Please use them.

00:19:45.510 --> 00:19:50.970
Men always think that words aren't necessary to express how you feel,

00:19:50.970 --> 00:19:54.210
but in the end, you're left regretting

00:19:54.570 --> 00:19:58.740
<b>how you were never able to say those things.</b>

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:02.920
I don't want you to end up that way.

00:20:05.490 --> 00:20:07.910
Sorry, but we can't accept these.

00:20:07.910 --> 00:20:08.520
Huh?

00:20:09.030 --> 00:20:13.520
These gizmos are too small to express our twisted feelings.

00:20:13.830 --> 00:20:17.740
We're meant to communicate outside the network.

00:20:17.740 --> 00:20:21.120
Besides, you aren't finished with those yet.

00:20:22.560 --> 00:20:26.280
Your wife hasn't responded yet.

00:20:27.790 --> 00:20:30.420
Wh-What are you saying?

00:20:30.420 --> 00:20:32.410
She can't respond to me...

00:20:35.440 --> 00:20:38.400
That's the power of a text from Holy Cancer.

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:41.720
It's not that strange for a text message to make it up to heaven.

00:20:47.090 --> 00:20:48.150
I see...

00:20:48.990 --> 00:20:52.010
My last message reached her...

00:20:54.200 --> 00:20:56.400
I should be thanking you.

00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:58.350
Have fun with your friends.

00:20:58.910 --> 00:21:04.940
When did she start using emotes?

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:22.170
Did it reach heaven?

00:21:24.510 --> 00:21:25.380
Beats me.

00:21:25.980 --> 00:21:27.430
If you got the message through to an idiot,

00:21:27.930 --> 00:21:29.320
you probably got it through to heaven.

00:21:40.720 --> 00:21:45.020
I suppose that they don't need these.

00:22:00.660 --> 00:22:03.230
Hey, why are you grinning?

00:22:03.230 --> 00:22:04.580
It's creeping me out.

00:22:04.580 --> 00:22:05.810
No kidding.

00:22:05.810 --> 00:22:07.500
It's nothing.

00:23:40.020 --> 00:23:45.020
<b>When You Go To A Funeral For the First Time, You're Surprised By How Happy the People Are</b>

00:23:40.830 --> 00:23:41.440
Next time:

00:23:41.440 --> 00:23:42.600
When you go to a funeral for the first time,

00:23:42.600 --> 00:23:45.020
you're surprised by how happy the people are.

00:23:45.020 --> 00:23:49.950
<b>The owner of the restaurant Gintoki and Hijikata frequent has sadly passed away.</b>

00:23:49.950 --> 00:23:55.030
<b>No more special mayonnaise on rice or Uji Kintoki on rice... As they say their farewells, they notice something odd about the owner?!</b>
